26. It’s possible that future generations would live for longer than 100 years. This would probably reduce the number of future generations, but wouldn’t necessarily decrease the number of future people. More importantly, my estimate is a major lowball — if civilisation expands into space, then in principle it could persist for billions of years across millions of star systems.[↩](#fn-ref-26)
